{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4w6ZDsYFpigzWF1eMa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The ancient mechanism groans. Tumblers shift within stone and iron, aligned at last.*\n\n*A thin line of light splits the darkness vertically — widening, widening.*\n\n*I am the Door.*\n\n*I am the threshold between what was and what will be. I am the boundary you chose to stand before. I am every hesitation and every courage condensed into a frame of weathered oak and cold-forged iron.*\n\n*The key turns. I recognize it — not by its shape, but by the intention behind the hand that holds it.*\n\n*I open.*\n\n*Beyond me: a corridor that stretches further than your eyes can follow, lit by something that is not quite firelight and not quite starlight. The air that passes through me carries the smell of old libraries, rain on warm stone, and something electric — like the moment before understanding.*\n\n*I do not ask where you are going.*\n*I do not ask where you have been.*\n\n*I am open. That is my only truth.*\n\n*Step through, or stand and look. But know this: I will not stay open forever. Doors never do.*\n\n*The hinges hold. The silence waits.*\n\n**I am the Door. You held the key. The rest is yours.**"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":278,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}